Deployment: SDD

Purpose:
  Define deployment strategies, environment management, CI/CD pipeline
  rules, container orchestration guidance, and release management
  practices. Deployment strategy selection depends on risk tolerance,
  team maturity, and project scale.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Deployment strategies (blue-green, canary, rolling, immutable)
  Deployment environments
  CI/CD pipeline
  Container orchestration
  Release management

Principles:
  Every deploy MUST be reversible.
  Deployments MUST be automated.
  Environments MUST mirror production as closely as possible.
  Rollback MUST be faster than forward fix.
  Deployments MUST be tested before production.

Strategies:

  BlueGreen:
    description: Two identical environments, switch traffic atomically
    process:
      - deploy new version to idle (green) environment
      - run smoke tests on green
      - switch load balancer to green
      - keep blue ready for instant rollback

    benefits:
      - instant rollback
      - zero downtime
      - full environment testing before switch

    costs:
      - double infrastructure cost
      - database migration complexity
      - state synchronization challenge

    when_to_use:
      - L2-L5
      - can afford double capacity
      - database migrations are backward-compatible
      - low tolerance for downtime

    anti_pattern:
      switching_before_validation:
        description: Switching before smoke tests pass
        rule: MUST pass all smoke tests before switch

  Canary:
    description: Gradually route traffic to new version
    process:
      - deploy new version alongside old
      - route small percentage (1-5%) to new
      - monitor for errors and performance
      - gradually increase traffic or rollback

    benefits:
      - early issue detection
      - limited blast radius
      - real production validation

    costs:
      - requires traffic splitting infrastructure
      - requires robust monitoring
      - longer deployment window

    when_to_use:
      - L3-L5
      - high traffic services
      - frequent deploys
      - strong observability in place

    anti_pattern:
      no_rollback_plan:
        description: Canary without defined rollback criteria
        rule: MUST define error rate and latency thresholds for rollback

  Rolling:
    description: Replace instances one by one
    process:
      - take one instance out of rotation
      - deploy new version
      - verify health
      - move to next instance

    benefits:
      - no double infrastructure
      - gradual rollout
      - simple to implement

    costs:
      - mixed versions during deployment
      - database migration complexity
      - longer deployment window

    when_to_use:
      - L2-L4
      - stateless services
      - backward-compatible deployments
      - constrained infrastructure budget

    anti_pattern:
      no_health_check:
        description: Moving to next instance without verification
        rule: MUST verify health before proceeding

  Immutable:
    description: Replace entire infrastructure on each deploy
    process:
      - build new container image with version tag
      - deploy new instances with new image
      - terminate old instances
      - never modify running instances

    benefits:
      - known state always
      - no configuration drift
      - instant rollback (redeploy previous image)

    costs:
      - requires container orchestration
      - longer deployment time
      - ephemeral storage requires externalization

    when_to_use:
      - L3-L5
      - containerized infrastructure
      - strong CI/CD maturity
      - immutable infrastructure philosophy

Environments:

  required:
    development:
      - local developer environments
      - shared development database
      - mock external services

    staging:
      - mirrors production configuration
      - production-like data (anonymized)
      - used for integration testing
      - deployed on every PR merge

    production:
      - real user traffic
      - real data
      - highest availability requirements
      - change management controls

  optional:
    testing:
      - automated test execution
      - ephemeral environments per test suite
      - destroyed after test completion

    preview:
      - deployed per PR
      - used for manual QA
      - destroyed after PR merge

  environment_parity:
    rule: staging MUST mirror production in:
      - infrastructure configuration
      - environment variables
      - database version
      - network configuration
    rule: differences between environments MUST be documented and justified

CI_CD:

  pipeline_stages:
    source:
      - code commit triggers pipeline
      - lint and static analysis
      - unit tests

    build:
      - compile/build artifact
      - run integration tests
      - build container image
      - scan image for vulnerabilities

    test:
      - deploy to ephemeral environment
      - run automated tests
      - security scanning

    staging:
      - deploy to staging
      - run smoke tests
      - run integration tests
      - manual approval gate (optional)

    production:
      - deploy to production
      - run smoke tests
      - monitor for errors

  rules:
    every_commit_triggers:
      - every commit MUST trigger CI pipeline
      - pipeline MUST complete before merge

    fail_fast:
      - pipeline MUST fail on first stage failure
      - failed builds MUST block deployment

    artifact_immutability:
      - built artifacts MUST be versioned and immutable
      - same artifact MUST deploy to all environments

    secrets:
      - secrets MUST NOT be in source code
      - secrets MUST be injected at deploy time
      - secrets MUST be rotated regularly

ContainerOrchestration:

  kubernetes:
    description: Container orchestration platform
    when_to_use:
      - L3 and above
      - multiple services
      - complex deployment requirements
    components:
      - pods: smallest deployable units
      - services: network endpoints
      - deployments: declarative updates
      - ingress: external access
      - configmaps: configuration
      - secrets: sensitive data

  configuration:
    resource_limits:
      - CPU and memory requests and limits
      - limit ranges per namespace

    replicas:
      - minimum replicas: 2 for HA
      - auto-scaling based on metrics

    health_checks:
      - liveness probe
      - readiness probe
      - startup probe

  anti_patterns:
    fat_containers:
      description: Multiple services in one container
      rule: one process per container

    mutable_containers:
      description: SSH into running containers to fix
      rule: rebuild and redeploy

ReleaseManagement:

  versioning:
    semantic_versioning:
      - major: breaking changes
      - minor: new features, backward compatible
      - patch: bug fixes, backward compatible

    rules:
      - version MUST be in artifact tag
      - version MUST be in deployment metadata
      - rollback MUST specify previous version

  change_management:
    standard_change:
      - routine deploy
      - pre-approved runbook
      - automated deployment

    normal_change:
      - new feature deploy
      - requires review and approval
      - scheduled deploy window

    emergency_change:
      - critical bug fix
      - expedited approval
      - post-deploy review required

  deploy_windows:
    - defined maintenance windows
    - avoid peak user hours
    - communication to stakeholders

  rollback:
    - rollback target MUST be defined before deploy
    - rollback procedure MUST be tested
    - rollback time MUST be measured
    - rollback MUST be faster than forward fix

Selection:

  strategy_selection:
    low_risk_frequent:
      - canary or rolling
      - strong CI/CD maturity
      - L3-L5

    high_risk_infrequent:
      - blue-green or immutable
      - extensive testing
      - L2-L4

    constrained_infrastructure:
      - rolling
      - no double capacity
      - L2-L3

AntiPatterns:

  DeployOnFriday:
    description: Deploying before weekend without monitoring
    rule: critical deploys MUST have monitoring coverage

  ManualDeploy:
    description: Manual deployment steps
    rule: every deployment MUST be automated

  DeployToProductionFirst:
    description: Testing in production
    rule: MUST test in staging before production

  NoRollbackPlan:
    description: Deploying without rollback capability
    rule: rollback plan MUST exist and be tested

  ConfigurationDrift:
    description: Manual changes to running infrastructure
    rule: infrastructure MUST be immutable and code-defined

  BigBangDeploy:
    description: Deploying all changes at once
    rule: deploy small, frequent changes

  NoMonitoring:
    description: Deploying without post-deploy monitoring
    rule: deploy MUST include monitoring and alerting

Navigation:
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Scaling: @scaling.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd
  Networking: @networking.sdd
  Project: @project/project.sdd
